<title>LITHUANIA: YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on 91-day Lithuanian</p>
<p>Treasury bills on Monday and all of the 50 million litas issue</p>
<p>was sold as it was oversubscribed, the country's central bank</p>
<p>said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 9.21 percent, down from the 9.37</p>
<p>percent offered to buyers at the last auction for 91-day paper</p>
<p>on May 19.</p>
<p>The settlement date for the issue is May 29 and the bills</p>
<p>mature on August 28.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas unless otherwise</p>
<p>indicated.</p>
<p>SOLD  DEMAND  MATURITY  MIN/MAX YIELD  AV.YIELD  LAST AV.YIELD</p>
<p>50    92.216  91-DAYS     8.90/9.37	9.21	  9.37</p>
<p>-- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
</text>
